-- =====================================================================
-- RRNetBanking — Slice 8: security
--
-- Loan products are reference data: customers read, administrators
-- manage. As everywhere else, no CREATE or DELETE is granted — the
-- back-office writes through microflows (lint CONV006).
--
-- ON PUBLIC PAGES: the legacy app had an unauthenticated front page
-- (1st.jsp, contact.jsp, services.jsp) that anyone could browse. Making
-- those anonymous here means enabling guest access, which changes the
-- app's attack surface and is flagged by lint SEC004 and SEC007. That is
-- a decision for the bank, not a detail to slip in, so the Contact and
-- Services pages below are behind the login like everything else.
-- =====================================================================

GRANT Banking.AccountHolder ON Banking.LoanProduct (READ *)
  WHERE '[IsActive = true]';
/
GRANT Banking.Administrator ON Banking.LoanProduct (READ *, WRITE *);
/

/**
 * Narrowing Slice 5's biller rule, now that IsActive is something an
 * administrator can actually change.
 *
 * Slice 5 granted AccountHolder an unconstrained READ, and the bill
 * payment page's company dropdown is a CLIENT database retrieve over
 * Banking.Biller — client retrieves DO apply entity access, unlike the
 * microflow retrieves that caused the Slice 1 leak — so an unconstrained
 * rule meant a deactivated biller stayed in the dropdown. The payment
 * itself was already refused server-side by VAL_BillPaymentForm's
 * IsActive check, so this was a bad-error-message bug rather than a hole;
 * it is still the difference between the back-office switch doing what it
 * says and doing half of it.
 *
 * Payment history is unaffected: BillPayment denormalises BillerName, so
 * a past payment to a since-deactivated biller still renders.
 */
GRANT Banking.AccountHolder ON Banking.Biller (READ *)
  WHERE '[IsActive = true]';
/

GRANT Banking.Administrator ON Banking.BillerForm (READ *, WRITE *);
/
GRANT Banking.Administrator ON Banking.LoanProductForm (READ *, WRITE *);
/
GRANT Banking.Administrator ON Banking.AdminSummary (READ *);
/

-- The back office needs to see the customer base it supports.
GRANT Banking.Administrator ON Banking.Customer (READ *);
/
GRANT Banking.Administrator ON Banking.Account (READ *);
/
